WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.467
Filtering early can reduce unnecessary work.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:11.497
Suppose a large sales table contains five years of history, but the analysis needs only the most recent month.

00:00:11.497 --> 00:00:19.376
If the filter can be applied before a large join or aggregation, Spark may have much less data to process.

00:00:19.962 --> 00:00:23.834
This does not mean we blindly move every filter to the beginning.

00:00:23.834 --> 00:00:26.774
The logic still has to remain correct.

00:00:26.774 --> 00:00:34.208
The principle is to remove data you know you do not need as early as the analytical logic safely allows.
